# One program that grows

The spine is `mages/chN.c`. Side examples (calc, car, temp, Person)
stay in `ch*/`. Do not add a new toy program when the next `mages`
snapshot can teach it.

Keep the author's voice in `.ms` files: first person, short, not a
textbook. Mystical wording belongs in the prose. Listings stay C
(`printf`, `NULL`, `struct Mage`).

Closed loop for every change: write the `.c` file, compile, run, paste
that output into the `.ms` file, then write the prose.

The twelve-chapter draft is in place. `mages/chN.c` matches the
outline in `intro.ms`. Chapter 10 is the payoff: load, grow, save.
Do not add a new toy when the next snapshot can teach it. If you
touch a listing, compile, run, and paste that output.

Habits to keep teaching: initialize, check `malloc`/`fopen`, pass length
with arrays, one dialect per file.
